&lt;p&gt;Here&#39;s a scenario every trader has faced: a stock breaks above resistance — picture perfect setup — you buy the breakout — and the price collapses back down. Fakeout. Loss. Frustration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What went wrong? In most cases, the answer was hiding in plain sight, right at the bottom of the chart: &lt;strong&gt;the breakout happened on weak volume.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Volume is the most underused weapon in a beginner&#39;s arsenal — and one of the most trusted tools of professionals. It&#39;s the one indicator that is &lt;strong&gt;not derived from price&lt;/strong&gt; — it&#39;s raw, real data about actual money moving in and out of a stock.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In this guide, you&#39;ll learn how to read volume, the four price-volume combinations that explain every market situation, how volume confirms breakouts and reversals, and the powerful volume-based tools professionals use daily.&lt;/p&gt;

