&lt;p&gt;Indicators are mathematical calculations applied to price and volume that help traders make sense of market direction, momentum, and strength. They don&#39;t predict the future — they help you &lt;strong&gt;read the present more clearly.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But here&#39;s the problem: there are &lt;strong&gt;hundreds of indicators&lt;/strong&gt;, and beginners often stack five of them on one chart, get five conflicting signals, and freeze in confusion.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The truth professionals know? &lt;strong&gt;You only need 2–3 indicators — mastered deeply.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In this guide, you&#39;ll learn the three most powerful indicators in trading — &lt;strong&gt;Moving Averages, RSI, and MACD&lt;/strong&gt; — how each one actually works, exactly how to trade with them, and how to combine them into one clean, simple system.&lt;/p&gt;

