&lt;p&gt;Ask any professional trader what they check first on a chart, and the answer will almost always be the same: &lt;strong&gt;&quot;Where are the key levels?&quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Indicators can be added or removed. Strategies can change. But levels are timeless. Whether you trade stocks, crypto, commodities, or forex — support and resistance work everywhere, because they are built on something that never changes: &lt;strong&gt;human psychology.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In this complete guide, you&#39;ll learn what these levels are, why they work, how to mark them correctly on a chart, how they flip roles, and — most importantly — &lt;strong&gt;exactly how to trade them with proper entries, stop losses, and targets.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Master this one concept, and you&#39;ll already be ahead of 80% of traders.&lt;/p&gt;

