&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fyers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Someone who wants research + advice&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Angel One&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Already deep in the Paytm ecosystem&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paytm Money&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;choose&quot;&gt;How to Choose the Right App for YOU&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ask yourself these five questions:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will you actually do?&lt;/strong&gt; Only long-term investing? Any app works. Intraday trading? Prioritize speed and order types (Zerodha, Upstox, Dhan). F&amp;amp;O? Look for option chain tools (Dhan, Zerodha).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How important are advanced charts to you?&lt;/strong&gt; If charts drive your decisions — Fyers or Zerodha Kite web.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Do you want advice and research?&lt;/strong&gt; Only Angel One offers meaningful research at discount prices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Are you okay paying ₹300/year AMC?&lt;/strong&gt; If not, skip Zerodha and pick any zero-AMC broker.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Have you tested the app yourself?&lt;/strong&gt; Download it, explore the demo, watch how it feels. The best review is your own experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pro tip:&lt;/strong&gt; You can open accounts with more than one broker for free and use each for its strength — for example, Groww for investing SIPs and Dhan for F&amp;amp;O trading. Many serious traders do exactly this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;safety&quot;&gt;Safety Tips Before You Start&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Whichever app you choose, follow these rules without exception:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Verify SEBI registration&lt;/strong&gt; on the broker&#39;s website footer or SEBI&#39;s official list.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Download apps only from official app stores&lt;/strong&gt; — never from links sent via SMS/WhatsApp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Never share your login, OTP, or PIN&lt;/strong&gt; — no genuine executive will ever ask for them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ignore &quot;guaranteed profit&quot; calls&lt;/strong&gt; — they are always scams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check your contract notes and statements monthly&lt;/strong&gt; to catch anything unusual.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable app lock / biometric security&lt;/strong&gt; on your trading apps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;faqs&quot;&gt;Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Q1. Which is the No. 1 trading app in India?&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By user base, &lt;strong&gt;Zerodha&lt;/strong&gt; is India&#39;s largest broker with over 1 crore clients. By downloads among new investors, Groww leads. But &quot;No. 1&quot; depends on your needs — use the category table above to find your winner.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Q2. Which trading app is completely free?&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Groww, Upstox, Dhan, Fyers, Angel One, and Paytm Money all offer free account opening, zero AMC, and zero brokerage on delivery trades. You only pay brokerage on intraday and F&amp;amp;O trades (max ₹20 per order).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Q3. Can I use two trading apps at the same time?&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Absolutely. There&#39;s no limit on how many Demat/trading accounts you can hold. Many traders use one broker for investing and another for active trading.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Q4. Which app is best for intraday trading?&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For intraday, you need speed, reliability, and good order types. &lt;strong&gt;Zerodha Kite, Upstox, and Dhan&lt;/strong&gt; are the strongest choices here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Q5. Which app has the best charts for technical analysis?&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fyers&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Zerodha Kite web&lt;/strong&gt; both offer full TradingView-powered charting. Dhan&#39;s SuperTrader also lets you trade directly from TradingView.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Q6. Is it safe to keep money in a trading app?&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Yes, with SEBI-registered brokers. Your shares are held safely with depositories (NSDL/CDSL), and SEBI rules keep your funds separate from broker funds. Stick to the major well-known brokers and follow the safety tips above.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;Q7. Do these apps charge for account closure?&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No. Closing a Demat or trading account is always free. If you stop using an app, it&#39;s wise to formally close the account to avoid future AMC charges.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Final Words&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here&#39;s the honest truth: &lt;strong&gt;the app matters far less than your discipline.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A great trader will make money on any of these platforms, and a careless trader will lose money on the best platform in the world.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So don&#39;t spend weeks overthinking this decision. Use the guide above, pick the app that matches your style, open your account today (it&#39;s free and takes 30 minutes), and redirect your energy toward what actually builds wealth — &lt;strong&gt;learning, practice, and patience.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The best trading app is the one you&#39;ll actually &lt;em&gt;use&lt;/em&gt; — starting today. 🚀&lt;/p&gt;

